{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|@file'\"' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"7:## 0. How to use this plan\n23:## 0.1 Standing rules from the brief\n54:## 1. The game\n92:## 2. Setup and verified ground truth\n108:node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\"),p=require(\"path\"),fence=String.fromCharCode(96).repeat(3);for(const block of fs.readFileSync(\"../PLAN.md\",\"utf8\").split(fence)){if(!/^(js|ts)\\n\\/\\*\\* @file /.test(block))continue;const code=block.slice(block.indexOf(\"\\n\")+1),file=/@file (\\S+):/.exec(code)[1];fs.mkdirSync(p.dirname(file),{recursive:true});fs.writeFileSync(file,code)}'   # writes §16's scripts\n144:## 3. The engine: what to use and the walls\n200:## 4. Architecture\n227:randomness from `w.rng('name')`; state in components; `Math.pow`, not `**`; every file opens with an `@file` comment, warns\n244:## 5. The world\n292:## 6. Core systems (all sim-side unless noted)\n294:### 6.1 Player\n300:### 6.2 Guns (`arms.ts`)\n323:### 6.3 Health (`health.ts`)\n336:### 6.4 Fever (`fever.ts`)\n345:### 6.5 Fire and wind (`fire.ts`, `wind.ts`): the star\n385:### 6.6 Stealth and AI (`ai/`)\n407:### 6.7 Vehicles (`vehicles.ts`). Verified recipe\n442:### 6.8 Buddies and the ledger (`buddies.ts`)\n452:### 6.9 Economy (`economy.ts`)\n460:### 6.10 Story engine (`contracts/`)\n480:### 6.11 Other world rules\n485:### 6.12 Use (`use.ts`)\n493:## 7. Weapons\n514:## 8. Story, cast, writing\n520:### 8.1 The Auctioneer's tapes (cassettes at places; 6)\n529:### 8.2 People\n542:### 8.3 The mercs (pick one at New Game; the others become buddies)\n553:### 8.4 Contracts (about 45–60 minutes; each 3–9 minutes)\n570:## 9. Look, animation, sound\n572:### 9.1 Art direction: the engine's native low-poly style, sun-bleached\n594:### 9.2 Animation: the engine's system plus new work\n605:### 9.3 Audio: code only, no audio files\n618:### 9.4 Polish: what \"complete and polished\" means here\n622:## 10. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n626:### 10.1 Controls\n659:### 10.2 First person without a closed door\n667:### 10.3 Screens and HUD\n685:### 10.4 Touch-only devices\n693:## 11. Title, attract mode, dev mode, About\n695:### 11.1 Title\n699:### 11.2 Attract mode\n708:### 11.3 Dev mode: Pause → Dev Mode (not in hub sessions)\n722:### 11.4 About/Credits\n726:## 12. Multiplayer\n732:### 12.1 The mode: **Contract Run** (`game.mode=contract`)\n748:### 12.2 The session flow (order matters)\n758:### 12.3 The lockstep core (`net/lockstep.ts`)\n782:### 12.4 The game on its own\n791:### 12.5 Own card\n795:## 13. Testing\n814:## 14. Build order\n832:## 15. Finish line\n834:### 15.1 Packaging\n838:### 15.2 Your own feedback\n842:### 15.3 Exit interview\n891:### 15.4 Coverage: TASK.md → this plan → proof\n924:### 15.5 Acceptance\n928:## 16. Scripts, verified as printed\n933:/** @file scripts/fetch-hub.mjs: downloads the hub's client, harness and protocol into .cache/hub/, where lint and format can't touch them. */\n946:/** @file scripts/bundle.mjs: builds the deliverable, one self-contained page named after the dev folder, in the folder above it, with the hub client first in its head. */\n997:/** @file tests/game/verify.mjs: the one command, node tests/game/verify.mjs [sim|page|hub|final], which prints only failures and a one-line count. */\n1039:/** @file tests/game/hub.mjs: plays the hub's harness over the deliverable in the four configurations the hub's own test uses, on a port the OS picks. */\n1084:/** @file tests/game/final.mjs: the acceptance check, reading TASK.md itself: names, title pick, one file, hub client and tags, the exit-interview file, no stubs, engine untouched, and in a browser: boots, music at 10%, touch notice, About. */\n1201:/** @file labs/game/net/stub.ts: step 0's session stub, enough of the protocol for the harness to pass while the starter runs; lockstep.ts replaces it at step 2. */\n1224:## Appendix A: TASK.md, sentence by sentence\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
