{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'wallClimb|superglide|gaits|mantle' engine/physics/movement/model.ts | head -25\nsed -n '20,100p' engine/gfx/geometry/registry.ts\nrg -n 'export interface EmitterSpec|export interface ParticleFields|velocity:' engine/fx/*.ts | head -20\nsed -n '120,147p' engine/sim/ragdolls.ts\nsed -n '465,510p' docs/GAME-GUIDE.md\"","aggregated_output":"11: * source value. Values marked \"ours\" have no source and are starting values for the owner's playtests. The gaits'\n21: * parse(MODEL_FIELDS, {}).gaits.sprint; // 6.604: 260 u/s\n43:  gaits: group('Ground speeds by gait, with a weapon out; `holstered` multiplies every one.', {\n164:  mantle: group('The mantle (the Apex Movement Wiki’s measures, and er-apex’s ledge test): a grab, then a pull.', {\n165:    reach: num(2.4892, 0, 20, 'The highest ledge it mantles from the air, its lip above the feet: the highest a climb reaches less its cutoff and end boost (273 − 147 − 28), 98 u.', 'm'), // prettier-ignore\n166:    auto: num(2.032, 0, 20, 'Holding jump on the ground, the highest ledge it mantles without leaving the ground: 80 u.', 'm'), // prettier-ignore\n173:    cooldown: num(0.25, 0, 5, 'No mantle within this of the last one’s end.', 's'),\n174:    window: num(0.15, 0, 5, 'The pull’s last part, when a superglide or a mantle boost takes.', 's'),\n175:    glide: num(1.8, 0, 10, 'A superglide’s speed, times the speed it mantled at: +80% over the holstered sprint.'),\n176:    glideJump: num(1.27, 0, 100, 'Ours: a superglide’s rise, the slide-jump’s.', 'm'),\n177:    boost: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'The mantle boost: a crouch press in the window glides too, rising a full jump, with no cooldown of its own (it starts the slide boost’s).' }, // prettier-ignore\n250:export const MODES = ['ground', 'air', 'mantle', 'climb', 'zipline', 'ladder', 'skydive'] as const;\n252:/** A mantle's phase: none, the grab up to the lip, hanging from it, the pull over it. */\n296:  mantle: { type: 'string', enum: MANTLES, default: 'none', description: 'Its mantle’s phase.' },\n297:  mantleLeft: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Ticks left of the phase.' },\n298:  mantleTotal: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Ticks the phase takes.' },\n299:  mantleCool: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'Ticks until it may mantle again.' },\n300:  fromX: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle began, the feet, east.', 'm'),\n301:  fromY: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle began, up.', 'm'),\n302:  fromZ: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle began, south.', 'm'),\n303:  toX: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle lands, the feet on the ledge’s top, east.', 'm'),\n304:  toY: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle lands, up.', 'm'),\n305:  toZ: num(0, -1e6, 1e6, 'Where its mantle lands, south.', 'm'),\n311:  wallX: num(0, -1, 1, 'The wall it mantles or climbs, its normal across the ground, east.'),\n315:  exitGait: { type: 'string', enum: GAITS, default: 'run', description: 'The gait it mantles out at: the one it came in at.' }, // prettier-ignore\nsed: can't read engine/gfx/geometry/registry.ts: No such file or directory\nrg: engine/fx/*.ts: IO error for operation on engine/fx/*.ts: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nexport function addRagdolls<C extends object>(world: World<C>): void {\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\n  if (!w.systems.has('ragdolls')) w.systems.add('ragdolls', stepRagdolls, { phase: 'readback' });\n}\n\n/** Gives actor `id` over to its ragdoll, as `hit` says (see the file comment); returns its component. */\nexport function handOff<C extends object>(world: World<C>, id: number, hit: RagdollHit = {}): RagdollState {\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\n  const e = w.get(id) as Partial<Body> | undefined;\n  if (!e?.actor || !e.animator) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'handOff(w, id)', value: String(id), expected: 'an actor with an animator (spawnActor with anim)' }); // prettier-ignore\n  if (!w.systems.has('ragdolls')) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: 'handOff(w)', value: 'a world without the system ragdolls', expected: 'a scene that calls addRagdolls(w) in its setup' }); // prettier-ignore\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\n  const { actor, animator: data } = e;\n  const given = vec(hit.push ?? [0, 0, 0], 'handOff(hit.push)');\n  const push = push3.set(given.x, given.y, given.z);\n  const yaw = actor.yaw;\n  if (e.ragdoll && e.ragdoll.rise < 0) {\n    for (const body of e.ragdoll.bodies) physics.setBody(body, { velocity: physics.readBody(body).velocity.add(push) });\n    if (hit.dead && !e.ragdoll.dead) {\n      e.ragdoll.dead = true;\n      reactTo(w, id, (r) => r.die(push, yaw));\n    }\n    return e.ragdoll;\n  }\n  if (e.ragdoll) removeRagdollOf(w, id); // getting up: down again from where it stands\n  const pool = pools.get(w) ?? new AnimatorPool();\n  pools.set(w, pool);\n  const animator = pool.get(id, data, { dt: w.dt }).pose({ at: feet.set(actor.x, actor.y, actor.z), yaw });\n`AnimationClip`, `AnimationMixer`, `defineMannequin`, `mannequinBody`, `MANNEQUIN_SLOTS`; types `MannequinData`.\n\n**Effects (WP 6.4)**: particles as data (emitters: shardfall's presets, the 2D engine's kinds, event effects), drawn with telegraphs on the floor, socket trails, bolts and camera shake by a view's effects; never part of the hash.\n`createEffects`, `FX_BUDGET`, `BOLT`, `defineEmitter`, `getEmitter`, `TRAIL_TINTS`, `ScreenShake`, `SHAKE`; types `Effects`, `EffectsOptions`, `FxEventPayload`, `FxStats`, `Emitter`, `EmitterSpec`, `EmitterLayer`, `ParticleFields`, `FxLight`, `BurstOptions`, `ParticleStats`, `TrailSampleLike`.\n\n**The feel kit (WP 13.4)**: courses, scripted runs of a scene and the numbers measured on them (`node x feel`); the runner and its verdicts; the owner's feel panel and copy as profile.\n`defineCourse`, `getCourse`, `listCourses`, `METRICS`, `runCourse`, `createFeelPanel`, `tunedSpec`, `profileText`; types `Course`, `Measure`, `Metric`, `CourseResult`, `CourseSample`, `MeasureResult`, `FeelPanel`, `FeelRow`, `FeelInspector`.\n\n**Camera modes (WP 2.5, WP 3.9, WP 13.8)**: a code to a camera, each mode's factory, and a game's own.\n`readCameraCode`, `createCamera`, `createShoulderCamera`, `SHOULDER`, `createFollowCamera`, `FOLLOW_RIG`, `createFirstCamera`, `createChaseCamera`, `createViewCamera`, `followCamera`, `defineCamera`, `makePose`, `poseForward`, `poseRight`, `poseUp`, `poseTarget`; types `AnyCamera`, `AnyCameraSpec`, `ShoulderInput`, `ShoulderSpec`, `FollowInput`, `FollowSpec`, `FollowCamera`, `FollowSteps`, `CameraKindSpec`, `Camera`, `CameraInput`.\n\n**The rig a view steps (WP 13.8)**: blends on live switches, the view effects, the view settings cam.*.\n`createCameraRig`, `rigOptions`, `CAMERA_SETTINGS`, `blendCameras`, `BLEND_TIME`, `createCameraEffects`, `applyEffects`, `cameraPlayer`, `apexFov`, `EFFECTS`; types `CameraRig`, `RigOptions`, `RigInput`, `CameraPlayer`, `EffectWeights`, `EffectsFrame`.\n<!-- api-map:end -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
