{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_258","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '25,77p' engine/sim/queryView.ts\nsed -n '101,120p' labs/game/attract.ts\nsed -n '95,112p' labs/game/sounds/page.ts\nrg -n 'check\\\\(.no page errors' tests/game/page.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"/** The physics queries, read-only: what presentation code may ask of the sim's physics. */\nexport type QueryView = Readonly<Pick<Physics, 'raycast' | 'shapeCast' | 'overlap' | 'probe'>>;\n\n/** The read-only view of a physics world. */\nexport function queryView(physics: Physics): QueryView {\n  return Object.freeze({\n    raycast: (...args: Parameters<Physics['raycast']>) => physics.raycast(...args),\n    shapeCast: (...args: Parameters<Physics['shapeCast']>) => physics.shapeCast(...args),\n    overlap: (...args: Parameters<Physics['overlap']>) => physics.overlap(...args),\n    probe: (...args: Parameters<Physics['probe']>) => physics.probe(...args),\n  });\n}\n\n/** The read-only view of a sim world's physics. Throws `PHYSICS_NONE` for a world without one. */\nexport function queryViewOf(w: object): QueryView {\n  return queryView(physicsOf(w));\n}\n          .map(\n            (x) => e.get(x.id) as unknown as { ride: { data: { kind: string } }; sceneProp: { x: number; z: number } },\n          );\n        const r = rides.find((r) => r.ride.data.kind === (kind === 6 ? 'boat' : 'jeep'));\n        if (r) {\n          e.actions.run('place', { x: r.sceneProp.x + 2.2, z: r.sceneProp.z });\n          e.step(1, { p: ['interact'], look: [-Math.PI / 2, 0] });\n        }\n      }\n      e.camera.set(\n        kind === 0 || kind === 6\n          ? 'cam3=fieldChase'\n          : kind === 4\n            ? 'cam3=fieldDown'\n            : kind === 5\n              ? 'cam3=fieldWalk'\n              : 'cam3=first',\n        { blend: true },\n      );\n    }\n    if (p && p.seat && p.seat.data.vehicle >= 0)\n      audio.play('sfx:field-engine', {\n        bus: 'ambience',\n        pitch:\n          0.7 +\n          Number(\n            (frame.world.get(p.seat.data.vehicle)?.ride as { data: { speed: number } } | undefined)?.data.speed ?? 0,\n          ) /\n            30,\n      });\n  }\n  last = frame.world.tick;\n  audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined);\n}\nexport const setBus = (bus: AudioBus | 'master', v: number): void => {\n  audio.volume(bus, v);\n};\n189:check('no page errors', errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_259","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('labs/game/sounds/page.ts');s=p.read_text().replace('type AudioBus','type AudioBus,type QueryView')\ns=s.replace(\\\"  const song = c.ending\\\", \\\"  const queries:QueryView|undefined=frame.queries?{...frame.queries,raycast:(from,dir,options)=>{if(options?.maxDistance\"'!==undefined&&(!(options.maxDistance>0)||!Number.isFinite(options.maxDistance)))return null;return frame.queries!.raycast(from,dir,options);}}:undefined;'\"\\\\n  audio.update(frame.camera,queries);\\\\n  const song = c.ending\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"  audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined);\\\",'')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/attract.ts');s=p.read_text().replace('{ blend: true },','{ blend: false },')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/main.ts');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"e.camera.set('cam3=fixed,548,18,730,156,-7');\\\", \\\"e.camera.set('cam3=fixed,548,18,730,156,-7',{blend:false});\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/game/page.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"check('no page errors', errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\\", \\\"const engineErrors=await page.evaluate(()=>window.__engine.errors??[]);writeFileSync('out/page/engine-errors.json',JSON.stringify(engineErrors,null,2));\\\\ncheck('no page errors', errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));check('no handled engine errors',engineErrors.length===0,JSON.stringify(engineErrors));\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n\n- A title screenshot after attract exit showed \"'`PHYSICS_BAD_ARGUMENT: raycast({ maxDistance }) got -104.488...`. Presentation'\"'s native audio occlusion walker computes \"'`end - inside` for its second ray without guarding a nonpositive range. The game now supplies a read-only audio query adapter that returns no hit for an invalid range, and updates the listener/query view before playing events. Large demo teleports also use camera cuts. The engine remains unchanged; the browser tier checks handled engine errors as well as page errors.\nEOF\nnpm run format > out/format.log 2>&1\nNODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=1800 npm run check > out/check.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
